-- title:
--   The (i,j) pullback chart lies over Spec R
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, with associated projective Weierstrass equation `W.toProjective`. Write $B$ for the quotient of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by that equation, graded by the images `projModelGradingCR W.toProjective` of the homogeneous submodules, and for $i \in \{0,1,2\}$ let $\mathcal A_i$ denote the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `HomogeneousLocalization.Away` of $B$ at the image of $X_i$, an $R$-algebra through $R \to B_0 \to \mathcal A_i$. Let `projModelStrCR` be the structure morphism $\operatorname{Proj} B \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, namely `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to B_0$. The cover `kwProjPullbackOpenCoverCR` of the fibre product $\operatorname{Proj} B \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Proj} B$ is the left–right product of the affine chart cover by the opens away from the $X_i$ with itself, and `kwProjPullbackChartIsoCR` identifies its $(i,j)$ member with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal A_i \otimes_R \mathcal A_j)$. The assertion is that, for every pair $ij$ of chart indices, the inverse of this identification, followed by the cover map into the fibre product, followed by the first projection, followed by the structure morphism, equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to \mathcal A_{ij.1} \otimes_R \mathcal A_{ij.2}$.
--
--   This records that the $(i,j)$ tensor-product chart of $E \times_R E$, for $E$ the projective model of $W$, is a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ when traced through the first projection. It is used by `WeierstrassProjManifold`-style chart computations, specifically by [`WeierstrassProjModel.perChart_addMorphism_pin_over`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.perChart_addMorphism_pin_over), where both sides of an identity over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ are precomposed with the inverse chart isomorphism.
